 "etapas": [
  {
   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "More than: 보다",
     "texto": [
      "To compare, you attach **보다** («than») to the thing you are comparing with. The adjective does not change.",
      "커피가 주스**보다** 비싸요 = coffee is more expensive than juice.",
      "You can add emphasis with **더** (more): 주스보다 **더** 비싸요. And 더 alone also works: 이 가방이 **더** 좋아요 = I like this bag more."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "The most: 제일",
     "texto": [
      "**제일** in front of the adjective means «the most»: 이 모자가 **제일** 싸요 = this hat is the cheapest.",
      "In written texts you will also see **가장**, which means the same."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Only and also: 만 and 도",
     "texto": [
      "**만** = only: 모자**만** 사요 (I buy only the hat), 물**만** 마셔요 (I drink only water).",
      "**도** = also: 모자**도** 사요 (I also buy the hat).",
      "Both take the place of 이/가 and 을/를."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
